h message; should pass extra={'keep_full_message': True}; preserve order/exception handling; _emit_logs puts list into _log_queue.\\\"\\n\\nI'll write that note with evidence ids.\", \"code\": \"note_text = \\\"environ.py: EnvVar is a non-data descriptor with __slots__ ('name','init','lock'); __get__ locks, checks owner.__dict__.get(name, self), calls self.init(os.getenv(name)), wraps exceptions as type(e)(f'{name}: {e}'), then setattr caches. Factory statics: int/float/bool/str/str_or_none/int_or_none/choice. New config should add a factory-created descriptor on envs class, e.g. EnvVar with lambda v: None if v is None else validate int>=32 raising ValueError. rearm(name) and rearm_all() re-set descriptors for refresh. logger.py: NewLineFormatter.__init__(fmt, datefmt=None, high_precision=False, use_color=False); format() calls super().format(record) producing msg with prefix, then multi-line prefixing replacing newline, then optional color. Message-length budget must be applied post-argument-substitution but before multi-line/color logic, using record.message length, without mutating record. Add keyword-only max_message_chars validated int>=32 (bool excluded) else ValueError; implement truncation with marker '...<omitted>...' replacing middle, keep ceil half of remaining head, rest tail. Respect record.keep_full_message is True exactly. _setup_logger creates/reuses _default_handler and always sets a NewLineFormatter; pass max_message_chars from envs config. init_logger adds _default_handler when non-deepinfer. stats_logger.py: _log_worker consumes queue via iter(q.get, None), sleeps based on dist.get_rank(), does logger.info(m) for each message; should pass extra={'keep_full_message': True}; preserve order/exception handling; _emit_logs puts list into _log_queue.\\\"\\nprint(write_note(title='Cross-module log budget mechanisms', content=note_text, evidence_ids=['ev-8554ade850ecb397d235','ev-246c6e73a88cb2c9edc3','ev-ef45633e339c9e5fd82f','ev-30754515034e43628968','